## FIRST STATEMENT OF {{client name}}

I, {{client name}}, of {{client address}}, make this statement believing the contents to be true and knowing it will be placed before the Court as evidence. I say as follows:

## Introduction

I make this statement in support of my application for a Non-Molestation Order made without notice to the Respondent. I will refer to the Respondent as {{respondent first name}} throughout this statement.

The Respondent and I are associated persons within Section 62 of the Family Law Act 1996 because the Respondent is my {{relationship}}. (Amend to state the basis of association, for example: we were married; we were civil partners; we were cohabitants; we were in an intimate personal relationship of significant duration; we have a child together.)

I seek the protection of the Court because I have suffered {{abuse types}} abuse at the hands of the Respondent.

The most recent incident was as follows. {{most recent incident}}

I fear the Respondent's behaviour will continue and/or escalate unless the Court grants protective orders.

## Background Information

I was born on {{client date of birth}}.

The Respondent was born on {{respondent date of birth}}.

The Respondent {{relevant factors about the respondent}}. (Substance misuse, criminal history, mental health or other relevant matters, if applicable.)

The Respondent and I were in a relationship {{relationship dates}}.

We were married/civil partners on {{date of marriage}}. (Delete if not applicable.)

We lived together between {{dates lived together}} at {{former joint address}}.

The children connected with this matter are:

- {{children}}

I currently reside at {{client address}}.

The Respondent resides at {{respondent address}}.

## History of Abuse

I set out below a summary of the abuse I have experienced. This statement is prepared urgently in support of an emergency application and may not contain every incident that has occurred.

I respectfully request permission to provide a further statement if more detail is required.

At the beginning of the relationship, matters were generally positive. However, the Respondent's behaviour gradually changed from around {{date or period behaviour changed}}.

## Controlling and Coercive Behaviour

The Respondent became increasingly controlling.

Examples of this behaviour include:

- {{examples of controlling behaviour}}

As a result of the Respondent's conduct, I felt isolated, monitored and unable to make ordinary decisions without fear of conflict.

## Financial Abuse

The Respondent was financially abusive towards me in that:

- {{examples of financial abuse}}

As a result, I suffered financial hardship and stress.

## Verbal and Emotional Abuse

Throughout the relationship, the Respondent regularly verbally abused me.

The Respondent would frequently:

- Call me abusive names;
- Humiliate or belittle me;
- Shout, swear or intimidate me;
- Make degrading comments regarding my appearance, intelligence or character.

Examples include: "{{relevant quotes or examples}}"

The Respondent's conduct significantly impacted my confidence, emotional wellbeing and mental health.

## Manipulative Behaviour

The Respondent frequently manipulated me emotionally.

Examples include:

- Blaming me for their own behaviour;
- Promising to change and then reverting to abusive conduct;
- Minimising or denying incidents;
- Making me feel responsible for the relationship difficulties.

I felt trapped and unable to leave the relationship.

## Physical Intimidation and Violence

The Respondent would often intimidate me physically. This included:

- Standing over me;
- Standing close to my face whilst shouting;
- Blocking my path;
- Threatening gestures;
- Damaging property; and/or
- Threats of violence.

On or about {{date of serious incident}}, a particularly serious incident occurred. On that occasion:

{{full details of the serious incident}}

I felt frightened and believed I was at risk of serious harm.

Following the incident:

{{police involvement, medical treatment, disclosures, photographs, reporting}}

## Post-Separation Abuse

Following the end of the relationship, the Respondent's behaviour continued and/or escalated.

Since separation, the Respondent has:

- Contacted me repeatedly;
- Sent unwanted messages;
- Called me persistently;
- Made allegations against me;
- Contacted my friends, family or employer;
- Harassed me on social media;
- Monitored my whereabouts; and/or
- Attempted to intimidate me.

The Respondent has also: {{details of ongoing harassment}}

## Recent Incidents

On {{date of recent incident one}}:

{{recent incident one details}}

On {{date of recent incident two}}:

{{recent incident two details}}

On {{date of most recent incident}}:

{{most recent incident details}}

## Current Fears

I ask the Court to grant the order because I genuinely fear for my safety and wellbeing.

The Respondent's behaviour is unpredictable and has escalated over time.

I believe there is a real risk that the Respondent will continue to:

- Harass me;
- Contact me;
- Intimidate me;
- Monitor me;
- Threaten me; and/or
- Cause me further emotional or physical harm.

I do not believe the Respondent will stop without intervention from the Court.

I therefore seek urgent protection and believe I am at significant risk of harm if an order is not granted.

## Special measures

I respectfully request that the following special measures be made available for any Court hearing:

- Screens within the courtroom;
- Separate waiting areas;
- Separate entrances and exits where available;
- Video-link participation where appropriate;
- Any other special measures the Court considers necessary.

## Without Notice Application

I respectfully request that the Court grant a Non-Molestation Order.

Pursuant to Section 45 of the Family Law Act 1996, I request that the order be made without notice to the Respondent.

I believe that there is a risk of significant harm attributable to the Respondent's conduct if the Court does not grant the order immediately.

I believe that giving notice of this application to the Respondent may:

- Increase the risk to my safety;
- Cause the Respondent to escalate their behaviour;
- Result in intimidation, threats or further harassment; and/or
- Deter me from pursuing the application.

In support of this request, I rely upon the matters set out above and in particular: {{reasons for the without notice application}}

I therefore respectfully request that the Court grant the order without notice so that effective protection can be provided immediately.

## Statement of Truth

I believe that the facts stated in this witness statement are true.

I understand that proceedings for contempt of court may be brought against anyone who makes, or causes to be made, a false statement in a document verified by a statement of truth without an honest belief in its truth.

