## Controlling and Coercive Behaviour

During the relationship, the Respondent became controlling and coercive.

Examples of this behaviour include:

- Monitoring my mobile phone;
- Checking my social media accounts;
- Restricting contact with friends and family;
- Repeatedly questioning my whereabouts;
- Demanding photographic proof of my location;
- Accusing me of infidelity without justification;
- Monitoring my daily activities.

As a result, I felt isolated, anxious, and unable to live freely.

## Emotional and Psychological Abuse

Throughout the relationship the Respondent subjected me to emotional and psychological abuse.

The Respondent frequently:

- Insulted me;
- Belittled me;
- Humiliated me;
- Made degrading comments about me;
- Manipulated me emotionally.

Examples include: "{{examples of remarks or conduct}}"

The Respondent regularly undermined my confidence and self-esteem. His behaviour caused significant emotional distress.

## Harassment

The Respondent repeatedly contacted me when I had requested no contact.

Such behaviour included:

- Telephone calls;
- Text messages;
- Emails;
- Social media messages;
- Contact through third parties;
- Attendance at my home or workplace.

The harassment occurred on a {{frequency of harassment}} basis and caused me considerable anxiety.

## Physical Abuse and Intimidation

The Respondent has subjected me to physical abuse and/or intimidation.

Examples include: {{details of physical assaults or threats}}

During these incidents I was frightened and feared for my safety.

As a result, I: {{police, medical treatment or disclosures}}

